e project","https://github.com/kekel87/pokemon-tactics","Complete pnpm workspace with game core, Pokemon data, Babylon renderer, UI and app assets. package.json requires Node >=24 and pnpm 10.32.1; pnpm install then pnpm dev. Code MIT; many sprites/tiles use CC BY-NC 4.0 and some effect particles have no separate license. Noncommercial fan project; read CREDITS.md.","Access type","playable","Play or run",[192],{"_51":193,"_26":194,"_178":195},"Play Pokemon Tactics","https://kekel87.itch.io/pokemon-tactics","Author-hosted browser demo on itch.io; choose Run game. Includes AI opponents and hot-seat play. An in-development fan project.","Game platform","itch.io","Guide format","disclosure","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[203],{"_51":204,"_26":177,"_178":-7},"Read the creator’s development disclosure","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[209,210,211,212],"Play a battle against the built-in opponents and test movement, height, type matchups and friendly fire.","Read the AI disclosure and CREDITS.md before exploring the engine and rendering packages.","Use Node 24 or later and pnpm 10.32.1 to run the complete workspace locally.","Change one tactical rule with an agent, then compare battle resolution, team setup and replay behavior.","AI workflow / foundation context","The creator directs design and architecture while Claude Code writes most code, tests and documentation with specialist agents. Pokemon data, sprites and some PixelLab artwork have separate credits and rights.","aiUse","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","Engine","Babylon.js · TypeScript","ai-assisted",[209,210,211,212],{"_51":204,"_26":177,"_18":199},{"_51":193,"_26":194,"_18":189,"_178":195},{"_51":185,"_26":186,"_178":187,"_228":229},{"_51":176,"_26":177,"_178":179},[117],"scope","complete-project",{"_231":232},"documents",{"_233":234,"_235":236},"en",[238,242,243,244,241,245,246,247,248,249,250,251,252,253,254,255,256,257,258,259,260,261,262,263,264,265,266,267,268,26